  "description": "Back-to-back containers: the kernel gave the next container's pid namespace the number the agent's had, so its first process (1 ms after the run, inside the 3 ms of both clock margins) and the previous container's last connection (1 ms before it) carry the agent's pid_ns and ns_pid. The certain anchor names the agent's init-namespace pid (its ppid, 4100); their init pids (4300, 3900) differ, so they are other processes, which cannot have lived while the agent did: not part_of the run and not unexplained (trace H4-other-process). The agent's own connection is H4.",
